---
import { milestones } from '../data/milestones';
---

<section id="how" class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="how-title">
  <div class="section-head">
    <h2 id="how-title">Three layers, one contract each</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Use one layer or all three. Each has a stable interface, so others can add modules, storage
      backends and compute targets without changing the core.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid-3">
    <article class="card">
      <p class="eyebrow">01 · Rust</p>
      <h3>Lineage and tooling</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        Read Nextflow's lineage store from local disk, S3, GCS or Azure. Diff and check runs, trace
        outputs back to their inputs, and expose it to agents as read-only MCP tools. Model answers
        are recorded once and replayed in tests.
      </p>
      <p class="tags">baqueano-lineage · baqueano-mcp · baqueano-replay</p>
      <p><span class="badge badge-accent">{milestones.foundations.version}, {milestones.foundations.status}</span></p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <p class="eyebrow">02 · Nextflow</p>
      <h3>Agent modules</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        nf-core-compatible processes such as RUN_METHODS and QC_REVIEW. Each one has typed JSON input
        and output schemas, and ships with evals and a pass threshold.
      </p>
      <p class="tags">meta.yml · JSON Schema · A2A</p>
      <p><span class="badge">{milestones.agents.version}, {milestones.agents.status}</span></p>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <p class="eyebrow">03 · OpenTofu</p>
      <h3>Infrastructure</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        One compute contract per target, in the user's own cloud account. AWS is the first target.
        A secure profile maps controls to NIST SP 800-171 and generates evidence for each release.
      </p>
      <p class="tags">infra/compute/&lt;target&gt; · infra/profiles/secure</p>
      <p><span class="badge">{milestones.infrastructure.version}, {milestones.infrastructure.status}</span></p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 24px;
    background: var(--nf-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--nf-line);
    border-radius: 14px;
  }
  .card h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk Variable', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
  }
  .tags {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono Variable', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--nf-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
</style>
